  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "El presente continuo",
    "@en": "The continuous present"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Para decir lo que está pasando **ahora mismo** se usa el presente continuo: **to be + verbo en -ing**. **I'm wearing a jacket** (llevo puesta una chaqueta), **He's buying a coffee** (está comprando un café).",
     "@en": "To say what is happening **ahora mismo** is used the continuous present: **to be + verbo en -ing**. **I'm wearing a jacket** (I wear a jacket), **He's buying a coffee** (I'm buying a coffee)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Negación: **I'm not working**. Pregunta: **What are you doing?** (¿qué estás haciendo?).",
     "@en": "Denial: **I'm not working**. Question: **What are you doing?** (what are you doing?)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "No lo confundas con el presente simple: **I work in an office** (siempre) frente a **I'm working now** (en este momento).",
     "@en": "Do not confuse it with the simple present: **I work in an office** (always) against **I'm working now** (at this time)."
    }
   ]
  },
