    "@es": "La ropa",
    "@en": "The clothes"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**Wear** es «llevar puesto». Para la ropa de ahora mismo: **I'm wearing…**. **Clothes** también es plural y va con **are**: **My clothes are clean** (mi ropa está limpia).",
     "@en": "**Wear** is «to be on». For the clothes right now: **I'm wearing…**. **Clothes** is also plural and goes with **are**: **My clothes are clean** (my clothes are clean)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Algunas prendas son siempre plural en inglés: **trousers** (pantalones), **jeans** (vaqueros), **shoes** (zapatos). Se dice **These trousers are new**, no «this trousers».",
     "@en": "Some garments are always plural in English: **trousers** (pants), **jeans** (jeans), **shoes** (shoes). **These trousers are new** is said, not «this trousers»."
    }
   ]
